0 Fixture: a minifig holding the camera, and the GRIP line that says so.
0 Expected: clean. Proves GRIP suppresses the hand's grip volume.
0
0 A minifig hand is a C-clip. It closes *around* what it holds, so in
0 LDraw the hand's solid and the item's solid genuinely share space --
0 about 800 LDU^3 here, well past even DECORATIVE_OVERLAP_TOLERANCE. That
0 is the fit, exactly like a pin inside its own hole, and there is no way
0 to place a held item clear of the fingers without it floating.
0
0 76382.dat puts its two hands at local (+/-23.69, 26.774, -9.898). The
0 half-turn below negates x and z, so relative to the torso the hands land
0 at (-/+23.69, +26.774, +9.898). Get that sign wrong and the item lands
0 in the hip instead, which is a real collision that GRIP would then hide
0 -- see bad-grip-not-touching.ldr for the stale-directive case.
0
0 The half-turn is also what makes the figure face +Z. 73200b carries
0 facing: -Z in connections.yml, so an identity matrix here would fail the
0 FACING check.
0
0 The red tile is not decoration. A whole minifig is decorative, legs
0 included, so with the figure alone on the plate nothing in the model
0 clutches anything and the baseplate itself reports NO JOINT.
0
0 !LDRCHECK GROUND 8
0 !LDRCHECK FRONT +Z
0 !LDRCHECK GRIP 30089.dat 76382.dat
0 !LDRCHECK FACES 73200b.dat +Z
